     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/manage-files/fileman-restore_from_trash
     */
    public function restoreFromTrash(string $path): array
    {
        /** @var RestoreFromTrashResult $result Validated against FilemanSpec::RESTORE_FROM_TRASH. */
        $result = ($this->run)(FilemanSpec::RESTORE_FROM_TRASH, ['path' => $path]);

        return $result;
    }

    /**
     * Save file.
     *
     * This function saves a file in a directory and encodes it in a character set.
     *
     * Observed: Destructive omission: PR37 review on cPanel 11.138.0.19 confirmed that omitting content, including
     * passing content: null, successfully truncates an existing file to zero bytes through both routes. A null variable
     * is not a no-op. Supply intended content explicitly and verify the target before calling; the client cannot
     * restore overwritten contents and never retries the write.
     *
     * Documented: Available in cPanel 11.44 and later. Disabling the File Storage role disables this operation.
     *
     * Documented: Saves a file using the supplied character encodings. The pinned description calls omitted content a
     * blank-file creation; the observed existing-file truncation caveat above also applies. Omitting dir uses the
     * currently authenticated user home directory according to the pinned source; no alternate relative-path base is
     * inferred. Content is sensitive and is form-encoded once in the POST body.
     *
     * Documented: Omitted fallback defaults to 1: save in the default character set if the requested one is
     * unavailable. Explicit false requests an error instead. Omitted source and target character encodings both default
     * to UTF-8.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:Fileman/save_file_content#GET (wire name save_file_content).
     *
     * @param string $file The files to retrieve.
     * @param string|null $content The new file's contents. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $dir The directory that contains the selected file. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $fallback Whether the function will return an error or save in the default character set if it
     *     cannot save in the specified character set. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $fromCharset The character set encoding of the `content` parameter's value. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $toCharset The character set encoding in which to encode the file. Null omits it.
     * @return SaveFileContentResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/manage-files/fileman-save_file_content
     */
    public function saveFileContent(
        string $file,
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        ?string $content = null,
        ?string $dir = null,
        ?bool $fallback = null,
        ?string $fromCharset = null,
        ?string $toCharset = null,
    ): array {
        /** @var SaveFileContentResult $result Validated against FilemanSpec::SAVE_FILE_CONTENT. */
        $result = ($this->run)(FilemanSpec::SAVE_FILE_CONTENT, [
            'file' => $file,
            'content' => $content,
            'dir' => $dir,
            'fallback' => $fallback,
            'fromCharset' => $fromCharset,
            'toCharset' => $toCharset,
        ]);

        return $result;
    }

    /**
     * Update buffer encoding.
     *
     * This function converts a buffer from one encoding language to another.
     *
     * Documented: Available in cPanel 11.44 and later. Disabling the File Storage role disables this operation.
     *
     * Documented: Converts an in-memory content buffer between character encodings; it does not name or save a file.
     * Content is sensitive and travels in the form POST body. discardIllegal controls discarding invalid characters;
     * transliterate controls conversion of invalid characters, with false requesting an error. Omitted options remain
     * omitted.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:Fileman/transcode#GET (wire name transcode).
     *
     * @param string $content The file's contents.
     * @param bool|null $discardIllegal Whether to discard any characters that do not transcode correctly. Null omits
     *     it.
     * @param string|null $fromCharset The file's current character set encoding. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $toCharset The character set encoding in which to encode the file. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $transliterate Whether to transcode invalid characters to valid characters in the new character
     *     set encoding. Null omits it.
     * @return TranscodeResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/manage-files/fileman-transcode
     */
    public function transcode(
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        string $content,
        ?bool $discardIllegal = null,
        ?string $fromCharset = null,
        ?string $toCharset = null,
        ?bool $transliterate = null,
    ): array {
        /** @var TranscodeResult $result Validated against FilemanSpec::TRANSCODE. */
        $result = ($this->run)(FilemanSpec::TRANSCODE, [
            'content' => $content,
            'discardIllegal' => $discardIllegal,
            'fromCharset' => $fromCharset,
            'toCharset' => $toCharset,
            'transliterate' => $transliterate,
        ]);

        return $result;
    }

    /**
     * Move a file to the trash.
     *
     * This function moves a file or directory to the account trash directory and records its original path so that you
     * can restore it later with the restore_from_trash function.
     *
     * Documented: Available in cPanel 136 and later. Disabling the File Storage role disables this operation.
     *
     * Documented: Moves the selected file or directory to the account trash directory and records its original path for
     * restoreFromTrash. The result contains the resolved original path and the trash leaf when present. The pinned
     * operation declares no rollback.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:Fileman/trash_file#GET (wire name trash_file).
     *
     * @param string $path The path to the file or directory to move to the trash.
     * @return TrashFileResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/manage-files/fileman-trash_file
     */
    public function trashFile(string $path): array
    {
        /** @var TrashFileResult $result Validated against FilemanSpec::TRASH_FILE. */
        $result = ($this->run)(FilemanSpec::TRASH_FILE, ['path' => $path]);

        return $result;
    }

    /**
     * Upload files.
     *
     * This function uploads one or more files to a directory.
     *
     * Documented: Available in cPanel 11.44 and later. Requires the File Storage role. Direct cPanel UAPI only; the WHM
     * bridge, LiveAPI and command line cannot send these files.
     *
     * Documented: Filenames determine stored names. The server renames later duplicate names, scans files for viruses,
     * creates a missing destination, and resolves relative dir against the account home directory; omission defaults to
     * that home. Permissions are octal strings (0644 or 644); a permission failure can produce a per-file warning.
     * These source statements are not locally live verified.
     *
     * Policy: Files must be a nonempty sequential list of Upload values; no path-string coercion, sparse renumbering or
     * per-file requests. Omitted query options preserve server defaults, including overwrite=false. Inspect
     * responseMeta()->uapiStatus() and all per-file results: either accepted status can include files that were not
     * stored. The required result object is validated under Unchecked; payload mismatches have outcomeConfirmed=false.
     * Any error can follow stored files; the client provides no retry, rollback, cleanup or ownership inference.
     *
     * Documented: Optional diskinfo byte limits and usage stay decimal strings, including infinity; inode counts stay
     * int|string. Additional human-readable display strings are retained. Absent fields do not mean zero.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:Fileman/upload_files#POST (wire name upload_files).
     *
     * @param non-empty-list<Upload> $files Files to upload, in order. Each filename determines the stored name;
     *     duplicate names remain separate parts.
     * @param string|null $dir The directory in which to store the uploaded files. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $getDiskInfo Whether to include the account's disk usage in the response. Null omits it.
     * @param bool|null $overwrite Whether to replace a file that already exists in the target directory. Null omits it.
     * @param string|null $permissions The permissions to apply to every file in the request, in octal notation. Null
     *     omits it.
     * @return UploadFilesResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the envelope was accepted but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the outcome is not checked.
     * @throws InvalidArgumentException If uploads are empty, keyed, invalid, or this handle uses the WHM bridge.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/manage-files/fileman-upload_files
     */
    public function uploadFiles(
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        array $files,
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        ?string $dir = null,
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        ?bool $getDiskInfo = null,
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        ?bool $overwrite = null,
        #[SensitiveParameter]
        ?string $permissions = null,
    ): array {
        /** @var UploadFilesResult $result Validated against FilemanSpec::UPLOAD_FILES. */
        $result = ($this->run)(FilemanSpec::UPLOAD_FILES, [
            'files' => $files,
            'dir' => $dir,
            'getDiskInfo' => $getDiskInfo,
            'overwrite' => $overwrite,
            'permissions' => $permissions,
        ]);

        return $result;
    }
